Cached the member pointer/index in locals and marked the invalid path as unlikely, so the hot valid path stays straight-line and avoids redundant member reloads. This preserves identical behavior while giving the compiler better branch layout.

```cpp
FIT_UINT8 Field::GetNum(void) const
{
    const auto* p = profile;
    const auto idx = profileIndex;
    if (__builtin_expect((p == NULL) || (idx >= p->numFields), 0))
        return FIT_FIELD_NUM_INVALID;
    return p->fields[idx].num;
}
```